                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "25b00a6c-5c09-310d-9a82-ba54d0e648e9",
                        "entry_id": "89c60ea8-ed1d-33f6-8786-5a36c8497a64",
                        "glosses": [
                            "матем. то же, что экспоненциальная функция, показательная функция"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd24d2e5-9933-4963-9d4e-45999ceee48f",
                                "sense_id": "25b00a6c-5c09-310d-9a82-ba54d0e648e9",
                                "text": "Свою раковину она строит в виде геометрически совершенной спирали, которую в учебниках именуют логарифмической: с увеличением полярного угла её радиус-вектор растёт уже не по линейному закону, а быстрее — по экспоненте, то есть степенной зависимости."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c7cf00fd-df2e-3860-b97c-a9c6821018f9",
                        "entry_id": "89c60ea8-ed1d-33f6-8786-5a36c8497a64",
                        "glosses": [
                            "матем. кривая графика этой функции"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c6db92d8-2eff-4162-892c-d4b4b665ca8f",
                        "source_entry_id": "89c60ea8-ed1d-33f6-8786-5a36c8497a64",
                        "source_sense_description": "показательная функция",
                        "target_lang_word": "exponent",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exponent",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0048b118-c27d-3898-8796-8c8c65a02c42",
                                        "entry_id": "c4c1b2d9-1e60-3a46-8596-479febb48bc8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who expounds, represents or advocates."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84b29434-d9db-4f7a-a9c3-fad82a84877e",
                                                "sense_id": "0048b118-c27d-3898-8796-8c8c65a02c42",
                                                "text": "Like attracts like,\" explained Mrs. Mailey, who was quite as capable an exponent as her husband."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b27b79a-5efd-41e4-988b-63ee0b42ae4b",
                                                "sense_id": "0048b118-c27d-3898-8796-8c8c65a02c42",
                                                "text": "To think of Kant as an exponent of virtue may seem to some readers itself novel and not easily associated with the Kant familiar to discussions of justice and rights."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "418b7eeb-89fe-3995-9bfa-37dce2a34952",
                                        "entry_id": "c4c1b2d9-1e60-3a46-8596-479febb48bc8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The number by which a value (called the base) is said to be raised to a power in exponentiation: for example, the 3 in 2³=8."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29f5d8c5-86d7-3ffc-8774-5d91d7acebab",
                                        "entry_id": "c4c1b2d9-1e60-3a46-8596-479febb48bc8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The degree to which the root of a radicand is found, for example, the 2 in ^(2])√=b."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cae434fa-91b6-4b11-a214-00fb44972d7a",
                                                "sense_id": "29f5d8c5-86d7-3ffc-8774-5d91d7acebab",
                                                "text": "A Power that hath neither the Signs #43; or - before it, is look'd upon as Affirmative, and if it be preceded by a Number that contains the Root ſought and its Exponent may be commenſured by the Exponent of the Root; namely for the Square Root by 2, for the Cube by 3, &c. it will contain the Root ſought."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2132c95d-49f5-448e-a0b4-6092a054307f",
                                                "sense_id": "29f5d8c5-86d7-3ffc-8774-5d91d7acebab",
                                                "text": "And univerſally the Exponent of the m Power, is m times the Exponent of the Root, and the Exponent of the m-Root (or #92;frac#123;1#125;#123;m#125; Power) is #92;frac#123;1#125;#123;m#125; times the Exponent of the Root."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91348e03-8a8f-49dd-9f7f-75514a654f74",
                                                "sense_id": "29f5d8c5-86d7-3ffc-8774-5d91d7acebab",
                                                "text": "The notation by which the root is expressed, is the mark #92;sqrt#123;#125; called a radical, placed over the letter, with an exponent to the left indicating the order of the root."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "177839b2-5226-3e76-9180-0e1503b051b6",
                                        "entry_id": "c4c1b2d9-1e60-3a46-8596-479febb48bc8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A manifestation of a morphosyntactic property."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cb48296-0859-4db2-806c-bd0e88d8398a",
                                                "sense_id": "177839b2-5226-3e76-9180-0e1503b051b6",
                                                "text": "However, there have been no examples presented of gender systems where the plain n triggers one exponent for gender agreement, and the male and female ns together trigger a different exponent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77ae5e59-8213-338d-be04-48b818314f5e",
                                        "entry_id": "c4c1b2d9-1e60-3a46-8596-479febb48bc8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The part of a floating-point number that represents its exponent value."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
